\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Deployed v3 architecture. $p_s,p_j,\mathrm  {dep},\mathrm  {spec}, \mathrm  {final}\in \Delta ^{3}$ are three-class probability vectors, whereas $p_n^{(1)},p_n^{(2)},p_n\in [0,1]$ are scalar neutral probabilities; $w_s,w_j$ are fusion weights, not model parameters. $r_\pm $ denote the positive/negative shares of $\mathrm  {dep}$ renormalised to sum to one. The two MegatronBERT-based heads share one frozen-backbone feature pass; the neutral specialist blends a judge-feature MLP with a corpus-trained MacBERT detector.}}{8}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
